  "level": 0,
  "ordinal": 0,
  "summary": "Digging Deep\nThe prospect of drilling for oil in the United States' outer continental shelf (OCS) has ramifications across not only the political spectrum, but the shipping world as well. The recent pre-election conversations regarding peak oil, energy independence and high gasoline prices have certainly raised some eyebrows. The advancements made to drilling technology, as well as the crude oil transportation systems have afforded the upstream side of the business more choices with respect to exploration, recovery of crude oil and distribution in deeper waters, while continuing to preserve the environment.",
